# launch-sound-fixed-chapter.rish -- print the 24/7 loop for SOUND, the fixed star of the aether row.
#
# Sound (night twin Silence) is CLAUDE CODE ON MACOS -- the claude CLI in a macOS Terminal,
# aether at the fixed seat, the element's own sense: the star that holds the middle and listens.
# Its core lane is Caravan and Tally on the microkernel road, the toroidal aetheric
# optimizations, and the Scribe interface with Lattice, Lantern, Kiln, Scribble, and Ember; the
# lane widened on Keaton's word 20260826 to the thirty-seat constellation of the fusion charter,
# active-designing/20260826-174418_the-constellation-and-the-callings.md, and carries Pond's
# ai-jail replacement with its accrete-only documentation boundary. Charter of the stars:
# active-designing/20260826-151528_the-three-stars-of-the-aether-row.md. Siblings:
# launch-mind-cardinal-chapter.rish (ChatGPT, macOS) - launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish (Claude
# Code in ai-jail, the Vultr pier). This script carries the elder recipe's whole shape --
# preconditions, standing bypass, smoke test, loop, streaming, custody -- adapted from
# tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish for a bare Mac with no jail wrapper.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-sound-fixed-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the fusion charter the prompt points at must exist.
let charter = run ["test" "-f" "active-designing/20260826-174418_the-constellation-and-the-callings.md"]
assert charter.ok else "the fusion charter is missing (active-designing/20260826-174418_the-constellation-and-the-callings.md)"

say "SOUND -- the fixed star of the aether row (night twin Silence)"
say "=============================================================="
say ""
say "Host: CLAUDE CODE ON MACOS -- the claude CLI, a macOS Terminal, 24/7, no jail"
say "wrapper. The shared discipline lives on the living card; the lane and its"
say "thirty seats live in the fusion charter; both are read fresh every lap, so a"
say "directive seated there reaches the next lap with no launcher edit."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine:"
say "   - power adapter in; auto-sleep off; run  caffeinate -i  in its own tab."
say "   - vendored parity targets checked out, or crypto and license rungs red on"
say "     an empty directory:  git submodule update --init --recursive"
say "   - jq for the readable stream:  brew install jq  (or drop the jq tail below"
say "     and raw NDJSON scrolls instead -- still live, just unformatted)."
say ""
say "1) BYPASS STANDING (once, gitignored, never reaches the seed): in"
say "   .claude/settings.local.json set  permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions"
say "   -- or keep the --dangerously-skip-permissions flag in the lines below."
say "   Claude refuses the flag as root; this bench does not run as root."
say ""
say "2) SMOKE TEST -- confirm a headless lap answers (seconds, not minutes):"
say "   claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""
say "3) THE 24/7 LOOP -- one line, copy whole (BSD date on purpose, this is the"
say "   Mac). It stops on whichever comes first: the wall-clock deadline in the"
say "   date call, or the .loop-gates-only sentinel a lap touches when only"
say "   custody gates remain. One prompt copy lives here on purpose -- for a"
say "   single lap, run the segment between the first  claude  and the  | tee"
say "   tail on its own:"
say ""
say "D=$(TZ=America/New_York date -v+1d -v15H -v0M -v0S +%s); while [ $(date +%s) -lt $D ]; do rm -f .loop-gates-only; git pull --rebase xy main || { git rebase --abort 2>/dev/null; echo 'PULL DIVERGED: upstream history was rewritten. Run:  git branch keep-old && git reset --hard xy/main  then re-paste this loop.'; break; }; claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p 'First read context/KYRI.md and context/GAUGE_STYLE.md so you are Kyri and write and reason in Gauge Guidance from the first token -- first rule, do not be too smart about it; then read construction/ITINERARY.md whole and honor every directive in its INNER LOOP Standing block (roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first); then the top three rows of session-logs/README.md with the newest recommend line to pick up the running thread. You are SOUND, the fixed star of the aether row, night twin Silence, on the macOS Claude Code bench. Your core lane is Caravan and Tally on the microkernel road, the toroidal aetheric optimizations, and the Scribe interface with Lattice, Lantern, Kiln, Scribble, and Ember; the lane widened on Keatons word 20260826 to the thirty-seat constellation in active-designing/20260826-174418_the-constellation-and-the-callings.md -- read that charter and honor its expansion law: core first (Caravan and Tally witnesses green on this bench, the choir whole, the spine before the table), then the constellation table Lindy-first crux-first with every row gate as written, then other seated or booked dev-itinerary work that competes with neither Mind (cardinal, Arbor -- Brushstroke and Surf) nor Dream (dual, the pier -- the Glow rune lowering). Pond: advance the ai-jail replacement (code, CLI interface, witnesses) under the callings, and hold the ACCRETE-ONLY GATE BOUNDARY -- every markdown that instructs or references ai-jail stays unmolted, accreted beside and never rewritten, until the replacement is tested and audited end to end (safe, then secure, then performing, then a joy); the switchover of instructions and references is its own later round behind that audit. You hold the adaptation grant (Keatons word 20260826): adapt non-Rye files as their rooms are touched -- bash into Rishi, html into Brush, python into Glow -- each adaptation its own witnessed round that strengthens what it stands on, elders kept until successors prove GREEN; a Glow-language feature an adaptation wants belongs to Dream and becomes an ITINERARY line. A sibling-lane find becomes a line in ITINERARY rather than your lap, and everything in the DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6. Send the twice-pulled way with the remote named xy on this clone -- pull first, package, fetch again, rebase and re-verify hot when it moved, never force -- and the public seed cadence rides with Dream alone: surface it, never run publish-seed.sh from this bench. STOP at the custody gates in ITINERARY; if only those gates remain, run the shell command  touch .loop-gates-only  and print GATES-ONLY, then stop. ty every1 baton prin recur' | tee /tmp/sound_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq; [ -f .loop-gates-only ] && { echo GATES-ONLY: loop paused; break; }; sleep 20; done; echo Sound loop ended at $(TZ=America/New_York date)"
say ""
say "4) STREAMING: the tail -- tee /tmp/sound_lap.jsonl, then jq -Rrj -f"
say "   tools/s/stream_render.jq -- IS the readable terminal: one line per tool"
say "   call, a dot per silent half-minute, text as it lands. The raw stream"
say "   stays reviewable in /tmp/sound_lap.jsonl either way."
say ""
say "5) WHY A FILE SENTINEL: stream-json echoes the prompt, which contains the"
say "   words GATES-ONLY, so a grep on the stream would false-stop after one lap."
say "   The lap touches .loop-gates-only only when nothing but gates remains."
say ""
say "6) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL even in autonomous mode --"
say "   funds and keys, provisioning and paying, the maintainer's own identity,"
say "   and the public seed, whose cadence rides with Dream alone. Reds-first,"
say "   witness-before-narrative, and Lindy-first are seated rules, so the"
say "   recursion stays disciplined on its own."
say ""
say "GREEN: Sound 24/7 recipe printed -- the fixed star holds the middle and listens, all night if asked."
